      "target_cell": "G5"
    },
    {
      "conclusion": "Confirmed by code reading and by this probe: grid10_interface.py has no module-level mutable state (no registry/lock/counter) shared across Grid10Plan instances. Two independent frames claiming the same logical_cell_id is therefore structurally UNDETECTABLE by this module -- not because it is proven safe, but because the module has no notion of 'another plan' to conflict with. Any real cross-frame conflict guard would have to live in whatever orchestrator constructs/dispatches Grid10Plan instances, not in this ABI itself.",
